into an opponent's graveyard from anywhere, exile it instead.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2024-09-27","toughness":null,"type_line":"Enchantment"},{"cmc":4.0,"color_identity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{4}","name":"Vedalken Orrery","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","oracle_text":"You may cast spells as though they had flash.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2022-07-08","toughness":null,"type_line":"Artifact"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"If you don't have a commander, Command Tower's ability produces no mana.","oracle_id":"0895c9b7-ae7d-4bb3-af17-3b75deb50a25","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you have two commanders, the ability adds one mana of any color in their combined color identities.","oracle_id":"0895c9b7-ae7d-4bb3-af17-3b75deb50a25","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If your commander is a card that has no colors in its color identity, Command Tower's ability produces no mana. It doesn't produce {C}.","oracle_id":"0895c9b7-ae7d-4bb3-af17-3b75deb50a25","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once a player announces that they're casting a spell or activating an ability, no player may take other actions until the spell or ability has been paid for. Notably, other players can't try to tap that player's permanents to stop them from paying {T} or to stop them from producing enough mana.","oracle_id":"3608f1f7-8dc5-4dd1-ae91-c830e1de9529","published_at":"2022-12-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The controller of Vedalken Orrery can cast nonland artifact, creature, enchantment, and sorcery cards any time they could cast an instant. This includes on other players' turns and during the upkeep step, draw step, combat phase, and end step.","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2004-12-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This applies only to casting spells. It does not, for example, change when you may activate abilities that can only be activated \"any time you could cast a sorcery\".","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Although Darksteel Citadel is an artifact, it can't be cast as a spell. Playing it follows the normal rules for playing a land.","oracle_id":"8dc067bf-f78f-4ac4-b6e7-b305c42cf0bc","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a nonbasic land has an ability that causes it to enter the battlefield tapped, it will lose that ability before it can apply. The same is also true of any other abilities that modify how a land enters the battlefield or apply \"as\" a land enters the battlefield, such as the first ability of Cavern of Souls.","oracle_id":"94fac5fe-97d5-4c12-a80c-8efff9d853ae","published_at":"2020-08-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a nonbasic land has an ability that triggers \"when\" it enters the battlefield, it will lose that ability before it can trigger.","oracle_id":"94fac5fe-97d5-4c12-a80c-8efff9d853ae","published_at":"2020-08-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Nonbasic lands will lose any other land types and abilities they had. They will gain the land type Mountain and gain the ability \"{T}: Add {R}.\"","oracle_id":"94fac5fe-97d5-4c12-a80c-8efff9d853ae","published_at":"2020-08-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This effect doesn't affect names or supertypes. It won't turn any land into a basic land or remove the legendary supertype from a legendary land, and the lands won't be named \"Mountain.\"","oracle_id":"94fac5fe-97d5-4c12-a80c-8efff9d853ae","published_at":"2020-08-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A player's \"opening hand\" is the hand of cards the player has after all players have taken mulligans. If players have any cards in hand that allow actions to be taken with them from a player's opening hand, the starting player takes all such actions first in any order, followed by each other player in turn order. Then the first turn begins.","oracle_id":"f4e32fc1-1b8d-441e-8e76-71f19f98e925","published_at":"2024-09-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If your opponent discards a card while you control Leyline of the Void, abilities that check whether a card is discarded (such as Hollow One, or a madness ability of the discarded card) still work, even though that card never reaches that player's graveyard. In addition, spells or abilities that check the characteristics of the discarded card can find that card in exile.","oracle_id":"f4e32fc1-1b8d-441e-8e76-71f19f98e925","published_at":"2024-09-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Tokens can still die while Leyline of the Void is on the battlefield.","oracle_id":"f4e32fc1-1b8d-441e-8e76-71f19f98e925","published_at":"2024-09-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"While Leyline of the Void is on the battlefield, nontoken creatures your opponents control won't die. They'll be exiled instead. Abilities that would trigger when those creatures die won't trigger.","oracle_id":"f4e32fc1-1b8d-441e-8e76-71f19f98e925","published_at":"2024-09-20","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
